# Netlify redirects — first match wins, so order matters.
# Keep the analytics proxy at the top: it must resolve before any catch-all.

# ---- Analytics proxy ----
# Umami is served from our own domain so script-src can stay 'self' (no CSP
# change in the six files that carry it) and ad-blockers filtering the vendor
# domain don't strip it. Harmless until the <script> tag in index.html is
# enabled — nothing requests these paths before then.
/js/script.js   https://cloud.umami.is/script.js   200
/api/send       https://gateway.umami.is/api/send  200

# ---- Function source must not be publicly readable ----
# publish is the repo root, so without this rule the raw function source at
# /netlify/functions/*.mjs would be served as a static file. The live endpoint
# is unaffected: it routes via /api/assistant (config.path) and /.netlify/…,
# neither of which this pattern matches.
/netlify/*  /404.html  404!

# ---- Retired demos (2026-07-28) ----
# The three emoji-illustrated demos were replaced by four photographic builds.
# Every previously indexed form goes to the work section rather than 404 — these
# URLs still carry GSC impressions for the fake brand names, and a dead page is
# the one outcome worse than the wrong visitor.
/aurum-jewels             /#work   301
/aurum-jewels.html        /#work   301
/demo/aurum-jewels        /#work   301
/demo/aurum-jewels.html   /#work   301
/bloom-ember              /#work   301
/bloom-ember.html         /#work   301
/demo/bloom-ember         /#work   301
/demo/bloom-ember.html    /#work   301
/fade-district            /#work   301
/fade-district.html       /#work   301
/demo/fade-district       /#work   301
/demo/fade-district.html  /#work   301

# Canonicalise the .html form of the current demos. These must be explicit and
# forced: a ":param.html" pattern does NOT work (Netlify params match a whole
# path segment, so it captured every /demo/* URL and emitted a literal ":slug").
/demo/salt-and-iron.html  /demo/salt-and-iron   301!
/demo/the-orangery.html   /demo/the-orangery    301!
/demo/the-alder.html      /demo/the-alder       301!
/demo/kiln-coffee.html    /demo/kiln-coffee     301!

# ---- Service pages (shipped 2026-07-29) ----
# These four used to 301 to /#services because the pages did not exist. They do
# now, so the redirects are gone and only the .html canonicalisation remains.
# Forced (301!) for the same reason as the demos above: without the bang a
# static file at that path wins and both URL forms stay reachable.
/shopify-store-design.html    /shopify-store-design    301!
/local-business-websites.html /local-business-websites 301!
/ai-receptionist.html         /ai-receptionist         301!
/custom-built-systems.html    /custom-built-systems    301!
/ada-accessibility-compliance.html /ada-accessibility-compliance 301!

# ---- The crawler's identity page ----
# The scanner's User-Agent string points at /bot, so this URL is load-bearing: a
# sysadmin who finds the bot in their logs lands here, and whether it resolves is
# the difference between "researcher" and "attacker" in their judgement.
# Do not remove or redirect this while any scan is running.
/bot.html /bot 301!

