# ---- Cancellation and refunds (shipped 2026-08-01) ----
# /cancel must stay a short, guessable, permanent URL. It is the "simple
# mechanism" ROSCA requires and it is quoted in the billing disclosure and in
# the acknowledgement email, so it must never move or 404. Forced 301! on the
# .html form for the same reason as the service pages.
/cancel.html   /cancel   301!
/refunds.html  /refunds  301!
/refund        /refunds  301
/cancellation  /cancel   301

# ---- Short link for cold outreach ----
# /hi used to 301 to the homepage with UTM tags. It is now a real landing page
# (hi.html) that continues the conversation the email started, so the redirect
# is gone. Attribution no longer needs UTM params either: Umami records the
# /hi pathname directly, and the form carries a hidden source field.
# Emails already sent link to /hi, so they keep working and land somewhere better.
/hi.html   /hi   301!

# ---- Booking ----
# Every "book a call" CTA on the site points at /book, so switching the
# destination on is a ONE-LINE change here rather than an edit in five files.
#
# TO ENABLE: create a free Cal.com account with a 15-minute event, then replace
# the target below with the booking URL and change 302 -> 301, e.g.
#   /book   https://cal.com/brickwork/15min   301
#
# Until then it falls back to the contact form, so the CTA is never broken.
# Deliberately 302 while it is a fallback: a 301 would be cached by browsers
# and would keep sending people to the form after the real link goes live.
/book   /#contact   302
